r-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390930} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "518c7bd4-e0da-52d8-997d-673ca75771ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{(s+4)t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390935} {:answer/id #uuid "2ff97a43-f336-5953-ad0f-7734328a6b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-(s-4)t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390936} {:answer/id #uuid "16f58656-d9ad-55d9-bfbd-701b206d4ef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{(s-4)t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390937} {:answer/id #uuid "91cc341f-4e42-5a66-9854-8c99a495219a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-(s+4)t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390938}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390936} :answer-field/id #uuid "89e9f6b0-7444-50e6-83bb-1ea02dd6ef57" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "65e33f37-ed72-5eab-bd4d-b7d3ad4f22b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-331791" :question/problem "Consider a function $y(t)$ such that its Laplace transform is $L\\{y(t)\\}=Y(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Suppose we wish to find $L\\{{e}^{4t}y(t)\\}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{e}^{4t}y(t)\\} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-1}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-2}}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={{field-3}}\\,\\text{for}\\,{{field-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Starting from the definition of the Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{e}^{4t}y(t)\\} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{4t}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-4)t}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $Y(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t,$ where $s>{s}_{0}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-4)t}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t=Y(s-4),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\ns-4>{s}_{0}\\,⇒\\,s>{s}_{0}+4.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "5e8902fa-0758-5942-8a51-66f230a0e33d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549093}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549135 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ebfe2578-7c5f-5df7-9d72-39a56be2386e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/8d/8daba7e586feeff02624e5d0fb508c9d2adedb23d5a79fe329f83a42e1f8256e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368083} {:answer/id #uuid "8e2c1dfa-8219-593c-b78b-6240e600685c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/82/82d01729627b5871739120d2e512cf54610eaaf43f6f2f2c454b7e39803937a2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368084} {:answer/id #uuid "0d7c5a3d-eb7d-5081-ba8b-a26f602f1890" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/e6/e6d497165f1dbc9fd9db77e6a8943f6acd45262cb74ebafd4a418d612be884b7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368085} {:answer/id #uuid "134ca311-f8fb-5d46-8687-e4802cae00a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/a9/a902bac22ba86af8de8b49d5aba5bb34f35433230f303432e1f4327708f41a7d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368086} {:answer/id #uuid "63430f1f-817b-5c2a-bd77-427ce4f138a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ef/ef457f3f2030bd9399e707ea5bc32f9fe58aae29f848c270c5b971afd98315bd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368087}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368086} :answer-field/id #uuid "84509ec0-1233-5211-bf4c-8b7806b1f61b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2acfbcc3-d517-5f68-a1bd-d612fba90c87" :question/math-academy-id "q-332104" :question/problem "![](images/82/82d01729627b5871739120d2e512cf54610eaaf43f6f2f2c454b7e39803937a2.png)\n\nConsider a function $f(t)$ for which the graph of the Laplace transform $L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be the graph of $L\\{{e}^{-2t}f(t)\\}?$" :question/worked-solution "The first shifting theorem states that if\n$L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s),$\nthen\n$L\\{{e}^{at}f(t)\\}=F(s-a).$\n\nThis implies that multiplying a function $f(t)$ by ${e}^{at}$ shifts the corresponding Laplace transform horizontally along the $s$-axis.\n\n- If $a>0,$ the graph of $F(s)$ shifts to the right.\n\n- If $a<0,$ the graph of $F(s)$ shifts to the left.\n\nIn our case, to get the graph of $L\\{{e}^{-2t}f(t)\\},$ we must shift the graph of $F(s)$ by $2$ units to the left.\n\n![](images/a9/a902bac22ba86af8de8b49d5aba5bb34f35433230f303432e1f4327708f41a7d.png)"} :step/id #uuid "b04bf113-65a4-5948-a558-678fc8e34fe0"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549150 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221947 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80a2b3a2-2a1c-5657-9a0c-46c3d1d0b071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Scale the graph of $F(s)$ by a scale factor of $2$ vertically." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220291} {:answer/id #uuid "c68eb1a4-0e89-5167-8c50-da7595818ba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Shift the graph of $F(s)$ by $2$ units to the right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220292} {:answer/id #uuid "45a5925f-203c-5ff0-ba1d-13bd03e18a2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Scale the graph of $F(s)$ by a scale factor of $2$ horizontally." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220293} {:answer/id #uuid "52465464-3cc9-5d3e-be71-9ddda92ffee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Shift the graph of $F(s)$ by $2$ units to the left." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220294} {:answer/id #uuid "6b9d9e20-287a-52d4-ae92-343b1c4d6e2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The Laplace transform is unchanged." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220295}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186220294} :answer-field/id #uuid "87c83dc8-2008-503f-a501-9ad228213d1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220290}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2fa333ab-b95e-5e37-a5a1-bded577fcc62" :question/math-academy-id "q-332055" :question/problem "Consider a function $f(t)$ for which the Laplace transform is $L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s).$ How can we obtain the graph of $L\\{{e}^{-2t}f(t)\\}$ from the graph of $F(s)?$" :question/worked-solution "The first shifting theorem states that if\n$L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s),$\nthen\n$L\\{{e}^{at}f(t)\\}=F(s-a).$\n\nThis implies that multiplying a function $f(t)$ by ${e}^{at}$ shifts the corresponding Laplace transform horizontally along the $s$-axis.\n\n- If $a>0,$ the graph of $F(s)$ shifts to the right.\n\n- If $a<0,$ the graph of $F(s)$ shifts to the left.\n\nIn our case, to get the graph of $L\\{{e}^{-2t}f(t)\\},$ we must shift the graph of $F(s)$ by $2$ units to the left."} :step/id #uuid "e30ffbbf-6dc6-5d22-8ffd-fc6caa3397ff" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549135}}] :activity/title "The First Shifting Theorem of Laplace Transforms" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548349}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551466} :activity/id #uuid "c46cfffe-18b2-5eac-8e1f-91eedc4c8269" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050615 :topic/id #uuid "58ea9fa1-e1b7-56f7-a58d-173ed320b2af" :topic/math-academy-id 6369} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551385 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368088 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71126cdc-4db1-5d85-972e-cd3f7216926d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{5}{(s-1)^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368090} {:answer/id #uuid "1f938eca-5b97-5407-a40f-c988b2a16b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{120}{(s-1)^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368091} {:answer/id #uuid "9820ac7b-3cc2-5748-8cbc-e6f3462796e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{24}{(s-1)^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368092} {:answer/id #uuid "8afdd9ac-60ed-53f4-9d08-0c4a351de9b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{120}{(s-1)^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368093} {:answer/id #uuid "37dc610f-9fa4-543d-8aae-3cf583648376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{120}{(s-1)^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368094}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368093} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ff80550-7623-5ff1-866b-cae616e84c57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7b5c8893-14eb-5d02-a313-3aa760c297c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-332128" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{t}^{n}\\} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}, &  & s>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nuse linearity of Laplace transforms and the first shifting theorem to find the Laplace transform of $f(t)=7{t}^{2}+5{t}^{4}{e}^{t}$ for $s>1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the linearity properties of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{f(t)\\} & =L\\{7{t}^{2}+5{t}^{4}{e}^{t}\\} \\\\  & =L\\{7{t}^{2}\\}+L\\{5{t}^{4}{e}^{t}\\} \\\\  & =7L\\{{t}^{2}\\}+5L\\{{t}^{4}{e}^{t}\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given that, for $s>0,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{t}^{n}\\} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{t}^{2}\\} & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ L\\{{t}^{4}\\} & =\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first shifting theorem states that if $L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s),$ then $L\\{{e}^{at}f(t)\\}=F(s-a).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nL\\{{t}^{4}{e}^{t}\\}=\\frac{24}{(s-1)^{5}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{f(t)\\} & =7L\\{{t}^{2}\\}+5L\\{{t}^{4}{e}^{t}\\} \\\\  & =7\\cdot \\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+5\\cdot \\frac{24}{(s-1)^{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{120}{(s-1)^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis transform is valid for $s>1.$"} :step/id #uuid "34e3daa2-8ba3-59ec-8c00-c52a7eef4a03"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551395 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551330 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01421a14-fbdd-550a-bb28-30816a633bd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "W(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550373} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e2249c-de4b-59f7-8146-a8b2909f33c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "W(s-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550862} {:answer/id #uuid "e1a8eccc-9669-52a0-a6c4-8e5789eba8f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "W(s+6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550985}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550985} :answer-field/id #uuid "0be05dc0-5dcb-5229-97d5-3889f2b77acc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551069} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc516240-edf6-50de-a972-2d32bd44c276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "s>{s}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550886} {:answer/id #uuid "e60983fa-e6a9-5ac0-89a9-689d559fbabd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "s>{s}_{0}-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550993} {:answer/id #uuid "e9fce1b0-8710-5564-a541-83b6838d2cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "s>{s}_{0}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550999}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550993} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e04132d-f893-5504-93e7-bc8007db050d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-